      "seed": 1495333985,
      "version": 767,
      "versionNonce": 1901176527,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1750567883360,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. for each partition\n- for particular date\n  - for particular hour\n   -  group them by song id -> publish similar different location",
      "fontSize": 11.491803777343746,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. for each partition\n- for particular date\n  - for particular hour\n   -  group them by song id -> publish similar different location",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "NPOyPmCG_2YVipx_3X4gZ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6772.422239345514,
      "y": 2490.068773943876,
      "width": 346.3653888891638,
      "height": 216.33858252510285,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 80,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b1P",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1338485665,
      "version": 1070,
      "versionNonce": 825357551,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1750567883360,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\nso finally we have frequency for partition1 and we are sure , the song\nwhich are in one partition, will not be in other parition.\n\n\nafter this, find the top k. from each partition. \nand merge them.\n\nand emit this to kafka \n\n{\n  date: <>\n  top100: [\n     { songId: <>, date: <>, score: <> },\n     { songId: <>, date: <>, score: <> }....\n  ]\n}",
      "fontSize": 10.180639177651898,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\nso finally we have frequency for partition1 and we are sure , the song\nwhich are in one partition, will not be in other parition.\n\n\nafter this, find the top k. from each partition. \nand merge them.\n\nand emit this to kafka \n\n{\n  date: <>\n  top100: [\n     { songId: <>, date: <>, score: <> },\n     { songId: <>, date: <>, score: <> }....\n  ]\n}",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
