    },
    {
      "id": "fgLMIYBYwUOM-Kgt2lWbi",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5982.220424580341,
      "y": 3590.385253311862,
      "width": 968.4791870117188,
      "height": 740,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 80,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b5M",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 887238305,
      "version": 2406,
      "versionNonce": 2100967297,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "8mKLWM4OGFiESN6S2w3Ve",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1750576486241,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. in happy case orch consumer \n   -> check zookeeper, call worker with consistent hashing, sync call\n   -> if fail retry infinite, \n   -> if success -> mean it had updated its local window state\n   -> orchestrator send events like this\n   -> individual maintain window.\n   -> now they will flush -> to queue.\n   -> merger worker only one -> maintain 1 min window\n   -> consumer all events , update its state\n   -> finally flush to sink\n\n2. failure cases: \n   ->  worker crashes -> it doesn't matter for orchestrator\n   -> since it will pull the live worker from zookeeper and send request\n   -> if let say we maintain some threshold upto that not having servier\n   -> orch stop processing and tell the client. \n   -> if existing threshold it will send.. \n\n3. orchestrator stateless so not problem about crashing.\n\n4. what if worker crash before flush ?? \n   -> it will update zookeeper, if having threshold , orchestration\n      continue sending , but it will go to other worker\n   -> resource manager will get to this about this\n   -> it will riase alert to oncall, \n   -> if we have extra workder, it will assign that until. \n   -> will try to restart the server \n      -> if success stop consumer in repaced worked, it will eventually flush after timeout\n      -> add this worker -> it will read the WAL and flush and continue reading. \n   -> while flush it will checkpoint to persist storage -> before wal state, after wal -> update state -> after flush -> updat\n      state -> so it crash we can get to know, what was the state ,let say crash after flush, we will\n      get to know\n   -> to make more reliable -> have replica instance as well. \n\n5. merge is single instance, so it will replay in case of failure. \n\n",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. in happy case orch consumer \n   -> check zookeeper, call worker with consistent hashing, sync call\n   -> if fail retry infinite, \n   -> if success -> mean it had updated its local window state\n   -> orchestrator send events like this\n   -> individual maintain window.\n   -> now they will flush -> to queue.\n   -> merger worker only one -> maintain 1 min window\n   -> consumer all events , update its state\n   -> finally flush to sink\n\n2. failure cases: \n   ->  worker crashes -> it doesn't matter for orchestrator\n   -> since it will pull the live worker from zookeeper and send request\n   -> if let say we maintain some threshold upto that not having servier\n   -> orch stop processing and tell the client. \n   -> if existing threshold it will send.. \n\n3. orchestrator stateless so not problem about crashing.\n\n4. what if worker crash before flush ?? \n   -> it will update zookeeper, if having threshold , orchestration\n      continue sending , but it will go to other worker\n   -> resource manager will get to this about this\n   -> it will riase alert to oncall, \n   -> if we have extra workder, it will assign that until. \n   -> will try to restart the server \n      -> if success stop consumer in repaced worked, it will eventually flush after timeout\n      -> add this worker -> it will read the WAL and flush and continue reading. \n   -> while flush it will checkpoint to persist storage -> before wal state, after wal -> update state -> after flush -> updat\n      state -> so it crash we can get to know, what was the state ,let say crash after flush, we will\n      get to know\n   -> to make more reliable -> have replica instance as well. \n\n5. merge is single instance, so it will replay in case of failure. \n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
