      "text": "1. in happy case worker will consumer direclty\n   - consume event check its eventtimestame ( evet time instead of processing, accuracy )\n   - set window let say tumbing window. ( for simpliciy not taking sliding window  )\n   - set watermark for delay events. ( how much slide extend to cover delayed message )\n   - event received, reduce timestamp to tumbling window, like divide by,  if any delay with watermark\n    update state of previous, since by dividing we will have old timetample. else update current.\n   - write wal and update inmemory state.\n   - periodic trigger for every minute , it will delay by watermark time.\n   - after window + watermark\n   - call merger with aggregate state ( sync ),\n   - commit offset, same every will will do \n2. merger: \n   - same like worker maintain the wal, for each timestamp , merge\n     data and flush to sink ( kafka ).\n\n3. sink -> olap\n4. user search last 1 min -> get result. \n   \n\n\nFailure cases: \n    - how we are handling high surge or delay in kafka\n        - allocate more processor as per the event estimations\n        - allocate in buffer as well so that.\n        - still then use watermark, else it will be dropped and use\n        - is this really possible ? let say 10 service sending event to kafka\n        - why one service send after 1 hour. in this case better to do batch\n            processing consolidation. in of add event aggregate.\n            - we can setup consolidation service that will take those events\n            - and tell accurate time. but eventual consistency.\n        - let assume either get in watermark or drop with this. \n     - processor crash\n        - we are using WAL and also it wll do snapshot as well to external file system.\n                - then for high consistenct\n                    - we use file system db separate called as checkpointing managd by orchestrator(job manger). \n                            ( assume it gauranted of saving, until that node faile )\n                        else involve hdfs or s3 for this. \n                    - processor will send db inn back groud, if it crash rebuild from there it has inf about commit offset ad merging send.\n                      fetch from db ( checkpoint) and update kafak commit. if pending to merge resend notification kind of. \n                      merge source of truth is db now. if it crash fetch\n                      from there ( previous task by kafka tas manager) and generate and send\n                      for ui person, it will be incident like it will search last 2 min.\n                     and 12 , but last will be shown as 11:58 not lates.\n                    - usually we keep more buffere node so these situation probailty is very less\n                      if happen very fast to switch\n               - we can also use local file db, it will be very tough problem ( not sure what flink does. )\n                  for reliabilty make its replica,\n                 then weill require some distributed consensus algorithm. \n               - these are all task manager\n                - we can have one job manager which will kind of take care of these job.\n                - like snapshot and checkpoint, etc.  assume this as source of truth and will have\n                  make this as reliable as possible. \n                - merger once send when we have all local state in checkpoint. ",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. in happy case worker will consumer direclty\n   - consume event check its eventtimestame ( evet time instead of processing, accuracy )\n   - set window let say tumbing window. ( for simpliciy not taking sliding window  )\n   - set watermark for delay events. ( how much slide extend to cover delayed message )\n   - event received, reduce timestamp to tumbling window, like divide by,  if any delay with watermark\n    update state of previous, since by dividing we will have old timetample. else update current.\n   - write wal and update inmemory state.\n   - periodic trigger for every minute , it will delay by watermark time.\n   - after window + watermark\n   - call merger with aggregate state ( sync ),\n   - commit offset, same every will will do \n2. merger: \n   - same like worker maintain the wal, for each timestamp , merge\n     data and flush to sink ( kafka ).\n\n3. sink -> olap\n4. user search last 1 min -> get result. \n   \n\n\nFailure cases: \n    - how we are handling high surge or delay in kafka\n        - allocate more processor as per the event estimations\n        - allocate in buffer as well so that.\n        - still then use watermark, else it will be dropped and use\n        - is this really possible ? let say 10 service sending event to kafka\n        - why one service send after 1 hour. in this case better to do batch\n            processing consolidation. in of add event aggregate.\n            - we can setup consolidation service that will take those events\n            - and tell accurate time. but eventual consistency.\n        - let assume either get in watermark or drop with this. \n     - processor crash\n        - we are using WAL and also it wll do snapshot as well to external file system.\n                - then for high consistenct\n                    - we use file system db separate called as checkpointing managd by orchestrator(job manger). \n                            ( assume it gauranted of saving, until that node faile )\n                        else involve hdfs or s3 for this. \n                    - processor will send db inn back groud, if it crash rebuild from there it has inf about commit offset ad merging send.\n                      fetch from db ( checkpoint) and update kafak commit. if pending to merge resend notification kind of. \n                      merge source of truth is db now. if it crash fetch\n                      from there ( previous task by kafka tas manager) and generate and send\n                      for ui person, it will be incident like it will search last 2 min.\n                     and 12 , but last will be shown as 11:58 not lates.\n                    - usually we keep more buffere node so these situation probailty is very less\n                      if happen very fast to switch\n               - we can also use local file db, it will be very tough problem ( not sure what flink does. )\n                  for reliabilty make its replica,\n                 then weill require some distributed consensus algorithm. \n               - these are all task manager\n                - we can have one job manager which will kind of take care of these job.\n                - like snapshot and checkpoint, etc.  assume this as source of truth and will have\n                  make this as reliable as possible. \n                - merger once send when we have all local state in checkpoint. ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
