    {
      "id": "T0z6JzKdYHfdkz8fOytH1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5646.57618357431,
      "y": 5466.439223932313,
      "width": 1600.339111328125,
      "height": 2065,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b8w",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1562340022,
      "version": 2724,
      "versionNonce": 233036342,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1752376932019,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": " top k -> also its very fast. \n\n\n- eventual schema -> songId, timestamp, score\n\nflow of processor. \n- Happy case: \n    - read and append in WAL also write offset. can we improved with via Redis bitmap\n    - update the local in memory state. \n    - continue to do so next offset. ( remeber as of \n      now i didn't commit the offset, but as per WAL running. ) \n    - there is cronjob , it triggers every 10 second.\n    - it read the current state. state is nothing but songId: score, but here usnig\n      count min so its matrix , hashes vs width , in memory will alos have songIds.\n    - set the partition|timestamp -> top k songs. or what ever is require as per problem \n    - commit the offset upto that with help of WAL amd same upate in WAS that \n      this is marked. \n    - we can also periodically snapshot in-memory CMS to disk (e.g. using RocksDB or local file).\n    - This continues.\n    - offline upload to timeseries db via redis\n    - backend server for particular timestample\n    - fetch all partition value from redis ad merge them inmemory and \n       return to client. \n    - in worst case for old data reconsilation -> but see if really require here since it approx. \n\n- Error cases: \n    - processor crashed.\n    - let say orignal commit 100\n    - wal - > 150\n    - flush but not commit\n               - mostly duplicate isue. since retry, better to have commit first push redis and add status in WAL, so at\n                - recovery would ave ideally it commit but didn't flush. \n               - This ensures no events are lost (at worst, they are double-counted  CMS can handle small errors)\n    - crash -> \n        - solution \n                - wake up then rebuild from that wal\n                - another processor -> rebuild the state\n                  from 100.  we are alreay using countmin that approximate things\n                - make the replica of that processor state WAL\n                - or make this system reliable to share that state to other \n                  processor ( cold )\n                 - and replace it it will be done for all\n                 - bit tradeoff is ok with loss.\n        - these are very rare cases\n                - we can try few of our trade off\n                - here two options for client.\n                        - delay the tell it will take time to upload at state. \n                        - tell the 9 partitions data on UI\n                        - since period is small. \n                - if restart works do that. \n                - if not there should be automatic \n                    way to replace it with new and start\n                    hardly few seconds.\n            \n - rebalance\n        - reassign patition.\n        - periodically send snaptop to external statemagement. rockdb \n        - fetch it seen the commit offset in kafk\n        - and wit help of these generate. ",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": " top k -> also its very fast. \n\n\n- eventual schema -> songId, timestamp, score\n\nflow of processor. \n- Happy case: \n    - read and append in WAL also write offset. can we improved with via Redis bitmap\n    - update the local in memory state. \n    - continue to do so next offset. ( remeber as of \n      now i didn't commit the offset, but as per WAL running. ) \n    - there is cronjob , it triggers every 10 second.\n    - it read the current state. state is nothing but songId: score, but here usnig\n      count min so its matrix , hashes vs width , in memory will alos have songIds.\n    - set the partition|timestamp -> top k songs. or what ever is require as per problem \n    - commit the offset upto that with help of WAL amd same upate in WAS that \n      this is marked. \n    - we can also periodically snapshot in-memory CMS to disk (e.g. using RocksDB or local file).\n    - This continues.\n    - offline upload to timeseries db via redis\n    - backend server for particular timestample\n    - fetch all partition value from redis ad merge them inmemory and \n       return to client. \n    - in worst case for old data reconsilation -> but see if really require here since it approx. \n\n- Error cases: \n    - processor crashed.\n    - let say orignal commit 100\n    - wal - > 150\n    - flush but not commit\n               - mostly duplicate isue. since retry, better to have commit first push redis and add status in WAL, so at\n                - recovery would ave ideally it commit but didn't flush. \n               - This ensures no events are lost (at worst, they are double-counted  CMS can handle small errors)\n    - crash -> \n        - solution \n                - wake up then rebuild from that wal\n                - another processor -> rebuild the state\n                  from 100.  we are alreay using countmin that approximate things\n                - make the replica of that processor state WAL\n                - or make this system reliable to share that state to other \n                  processor ( cold )\n                 - and replace it it will be done for all\n                 - bit tradeoff is ok with loss.\n        - these are very rare cases\n                - we can try few of our trade off\n                - here two options for client.\n                        - delay the tell it will take time to upload at state. \n                        - tell the 9 partitions data on UI\n                        - since period is small. \n                - if restart works do that. \n                - if not there should be automatic \n                    way to replace it with new and start\n                    hardly few seconds.\n            \n - rebalance\n        - reassign patition.\n        - periodically send snaptop to external statemagement. rockdb \n        - fetch it seen the commit offset in kafk\n        - and wit help of these generate. ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
